        "original_id": "1ee768da-0d1b-5a99-869f-125eff973bf9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport, Cheyenne Regional Airport, Little Rock, Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming\n- Products: Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701\n- Concepts: civil-military airports, international airports, repositioning flights\n\nFacts:\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport has the identifiers IATA MSP, ICAO KMSP, and FAA LID MSP.\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is also known as Wold–Chamberlain Field and is a joint civil-military public use international airport.\n- Cheyenne Regional Airport has the identifiers IATA CYS, ICAO KCYS, and FAA LID CYS.\n- Cheyenne Regional Airport, also called Jerry Olson Field, is a civil-military airport located one mile north of downtown Cheyenne in Laramie County, Wyoming.\n- Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701 was an overnight repositioning flight with no passengers from Little Rock, Arkansas, to Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport.\n- Both crew members on Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701 were killed.",
